{"claim": "P01802's PCP encounter E003862 (chronic kidney disease stage 4) ran 15:26-16:26 that day, overlapping every reviewed access", "sources": ["G4", "L1", "L2", "L3"]},
{"claim": "The access came from D0050, a PCP workstation, and the identity graph links U0082 to encounter E003862 through department PCP", "sources": ["G10", "G9", "L1", "L2", "L3"]},
{"claim": "All three actions were query/read (A0237, A0335), consistent with front-desk lookup; no print or copy appears in the reviewed events", "sources": ["L1", "L2", "L3", "G27"]}
],
"risk_indicators": [
{"claim": "A 'last name' connection exists between U0082 and P01802; no fact shows whether they are actually related", "sources": ["G8"]}
],
"missing_information": [
"Whether U0082 and P01802 are related (the nature of the G8 last-name connection)",
"U0082's specific task, e.g., check-in for encounter E003862 or scheduling the follow-up PCP visits shown in G5-G7",
"Whether the clerk role includes record access for patients being seen in PCP"
],
"disposition": "clear",
"priority": "low",
"rationale": "Clerk U0082 accessed P01802 from a PCP workstation during her scheduled shift while the patient was in an active PCP encounter in her own department (G1, G2, G4, G9, G10). Actions were query/read only (L1-L3, G27). The last-name link (G8) is noted but does not outweigh the documented job context; relationship unconfirmed."
}

